+Migration 003 supplies persistent login rate limits. Migration 005 adds immutable PIDs, separate credentials and authenticated actor references. Member sessions validate active status, enabled credential and credential version inside the write transaction. Reset/disable and ordinary writes share Business locking; a stale concurrent transaction is rejected. Version 0.4.0 rejects the old shared password and team cookie. Existing local startup stays a trusted loopback operator workspace, without cloud synchronization or Member impersonation. Hosted import remains an operator task.
+
+Trusted operator commands from the workspace root:
+
+```powershell
+node projects/zuri-go/provision-members.mjs --cloud
+node projects/zuri-go/provision-members.mjs --cloud --reset ZGO-P0001
+node projects/zuri-go/provision-members.mjs --cloud --disable ZGO-P0001
+node projects/zuri-go/provision-members.mjs --cloud --enable ZGO-P0001
+```
+
+The first command provisions only missing credentials and verifies existing private handovers; it never silently rotates passwords. Reset generates a new private handover and invalidates previous sessions. Disable/enable also increments the credential version. A newly registered profile receives a PID automatically; only an operator enables its login. No self-service password recovery or email delivery is included. Disabling a profile blocks its sessions while inactive; use credential disable/reset to permanently revoke its existing sessions before reactivating it.
 
